Description: avcodec/bsf/h264_metadata,hevc_metadata: add the frame_packing option
 Add pass, insert, remove and extract actions for frame packing
 arrangement SEI messages. Insertion takes the layout from explicit
 options, then packet Stereo 3D side data, then stream side data. Write
 before each seek point, on non-key packets carrying side data, and when
 replacing later arrangements or cancellations. Temporal arrangements are
 written on every packet, using LEFT and RIGHT as physical eyes and the
 selected content interpretation to determine the constituent frame
 number. Packed or unspecified temporal views alternate in packet order,
 which requires display-order input, and restart after a flush. An
 explicit physical eye sets the phase for subsequent unspecified views.
 Reject forbidden quincunx combinations and nonzero content
 interpretation for H.264 type 6. Extraction leaves the bitstream intact
 and exports the last non-reserved arrangement in the access unit as
 packet Stereo 3D side data when its layout is representable. It does not
 infer persistence on packets without a message. Flushing resets
 done_first_au as well as the temporal phase, so display_orientation also
 treats the first access unit after a flush as a seek point. This is
 intentional because a flush starts a new input segment whose first
 packet may have neither SPS nor a key flag.
 .
 The new message has the arrangement id 0 and replaces only a message
 with that id. A persistent arrangement with another id, passed on by an
 earlier access unit, stays in force until its coded video sequence
 ends, so such ids are tracked and cancelled in the access unit that
 gets the new message (H.264 D.2.26, H.265 D.3.16). H.265 has no
 two-dimensional arrangement: a 2D description cancels them and writes
 none.
 .
 H.265 insertion clears general_non_packed_constraint_flag, and the
 sub-layer flag, in the VPS and SPS it passes on, those of the extradata
 included, because the flag forbids a frame packing arrangement in the
 coded video sequence (H.265 7.4.4). A layout that is first given after
 parameter sets with the flag were passed on is an error. H.264 tile
 format insertion is refused unless the cropped size of the active SPS is
 a multiple of 3 both ways (D.2.26). Extraction does not export a
 mirrored view or quincunx sampling other than that of the side by side
 and checkerboard layouts, which AVStereo3D cannot describe. Removal also
 removes the messages from the extradata, which comes without a packet.
 .
 The self-contained flags of a new message are those of the messages seen
 before it in the coded video sequence, because they are the same in all
 of them (H.264 D.2.26, H.265 D.3.16).
 .
