diff --git a/doc/bitstream_filters.texi b/doc/bitstream_filters.texi
index c6705bb..7aec54e 100644
--- a/doc/bitstream_filters.texi
+++ b/doc/bitstream_filters.texi
@@ -450,6 +450,89 @@ Insert mode works in conjunction with @code{rotate} and @code{flip} options.
 Any pre-existing Display orientation messages will be removed in insert or remove mode.
 Extract mode attaches the display matrix to the packet as side data.
 
+@item frame_packing
+Insert, remove or extract Frame packing arrangement SEI messages.
+See H.264 section D.1.26 and D.2.26 for syntax and semantics.
+
+@table @samp
+@item pass
+@item insert
+@item remove
+@item extract
+@end table
+
+Default is pass.
+
+Insert mode writes the message in front of every key frame, or in front of
+every frame for temporal interleaving, and replaces a pre-existing message in
+those access units. The layout comes from the @code{frame_packing_type},
+@code{frame_packing_view} and @code{frame_packing_quincunx} options, and what
+they leave unset comes from the Stereo 3D side data of the stream or of the
+packet, such as the one the Matroska demuxer reads from @code{StereoMode}.
+Without a type and without side data the stream is passed unchanged.
+This option describes an existing layout; it does not rearrange the pictures.
+For temporal interleaving, a per-packet Stereo 3D LEFT or RIGHT view selects
+the physical eye, with the content interpretation determining its constituent
+frame number. Otherwise the frames alternate in packet order, starting with frame 0
+and restarting after a flush. In that case the input must be in display order.
+An explicit view sets the phase for subsequent unspecified views.
+Reordered input requires a per-packet view description.
+Existing frame packing messages are replaced, including cancellation messages.
+The new message has the arrangement id 0. A persistent message with another id
+that an earlier access unit passed on is ended by a cancellation message in the
+access unit that gets the new one, so that it is the only layout in force.
+The new message has the frame0_self_contained_flag and frame1_self_contained_flag
+of the messages already seen in the coded video sequence, which are the same in
+all of them.
+Packet side data is applied on the packet that carries it.
+
+Extract mode attaches a representable frame packing message from the access
+unit to the packet as @code{AV_PKT_DATA_STEREO3D} side data, leaving the SEI
+in the bitstream. If several messages are present, the last one with a
+non-reserved arrangement ID is used. Cancellation messages, unknown content
+interpretations and layouts without an @code{AVStereo3D} equivalent do not
+produce side data; among them are a mirrored view (spatial_flipping_flag) and
+quincunx sampling other than that of the side by side and checkerboard layouts.
+Extraction describes messages present in the packet;
+it does not infer persistence on packets without a message.
+
+Remove mode also removes the messages from the extradata.
+
+@item frame_packing_type
+Set frame_packing_arrangement_type (H.264 table D-9).
+
+@table @samp
+@item checkerboard
+@item columns
+@item rows
+@item side_by_side
+@item top_bottom
+@item temporal
+@item 2d
+@item tile
+@end table
+
+Default is to take it from the Stereo 3D side data. The tile format needs a
+cropped picture size, with the crop of this filter applied, that is a multiple
+of 3 both ways.
+
+@item frame_packing_view
+Set content_interpretation_type: which view the first frame of the arrangement
+is.
+
+@table @samp
+@item unspecified
+@item left_first
+@item right_first
+@end table
+
+Default is to take it from the Stereo 3D side data, left first without any.
+
+@item frame_packing_quincunx
+Set quincunx_sampling_flag. Default is to take it from the Stereo 3D side data;
+it is always set for the checkerboard.
+A value of 1 is invalid for temporal interleaving, 2D and tile layouts.
+
 @item rotate
 Set rotation in display orientation SEI (anticlockwise angle in degrees).
 Range is -360 to +360. Default is NaN.
@@ -568,6 +651,90 @@ representable if the chroma is subsampled (H.265 section 7.4.3.2.1).
 @item height
 Set width and height after crop.
 
+@item frame_packing
+Insert, remove or extract Frame packing arrangement SEI messages.
+See H.265 section D.2.16 and D.3.16 for syntax and semantics.
+
+@table @samp
+@item pass
+@item insert
+@item remove
+@item extract
+@end table
+
+Default is pass.
+
+Insert mode writes the message in front of every key frame, or in front of
+every frame for temporal interleaving, and replaces a pre-existing message in
+those access units. The layout comes from the @code{frame_packing_type},
+@code{frame_packing_view} and @code{frame_packing_quincunx} options, and what
+they leave unset comes from the Stereo 3D side data of the stream or of the
+packet, such as the one the Matroska demuxer reads from @code{StereoMode}.
+Without a type and without side data the stream is passed unchanged.
+This option describes an existing layout; it does not rearrange the pictures.
+For temporal interleaving, a per-packet Stereo 3D LEFT or RIGHT view selects
+the physical eye, with the content interpretation determining its constituent
+frame number. Otherwise the frames alternate in packet order, starting with frame 0
+and restarting after a flush. In that case the input must be in display order.
+An explicit view sets the phase for subsequent unspecified views.
+Reordered input requires a per-packet view description.
+Existing frame packing messages are replaced, including cancellation messages.
+The new message has the arrangement id 0. A persistent message with another id
+that an earlier access unit passed on is ended by a cancellation message in the
+access unit that gets the new one, so that it is the only layout in force.
+The new message has the frame0_self_contained_flag and frame1_self_contained_flag
+of the messages already seen in the coded video sequence, which are the same in
+all of them.
+A Stereo 3D description of a two-dimensional picture has no H.265 arrangement:
+it ends the messages in force and writes none.
+Packet side data is applied on the packet that carries it.
+The SEI NAL unit written for an access unit has the TemporalId and the layer
+of its picture.
+A stream that is given a layout also stops declaring that it has none:
+general_non_packed_constraint_flag, and the sub-layer flag, are cleared in
+every VPS and SPS passed on, those of the extradata included
+(H.265 7.4.4). A layout that is first given by packet side data after a
+VPS or SPS with the flag set was passed on is an error.
+
+Extract mode attaches a representable frame packing message from the access
+unit to the packet as @code{AV_PKT_DATA_STEREO3D} side data, leaving the SEI
+in the bitstream. If several messages are present, the last one with a
+non-reserved arrangement ID is used. Cancellation messages, unknown content
+interpretations and layouts without an @code{AVStereo3D} equivalent do not
+produce side data; among them are a mirrored view (spatial_flipping_flag) and
+quincunx sampling other than that of the side by side layout.
+Extraction describes messages present in the packet;
+it does not infer persistence on packets without a message.
+
+Remove mode also removes the messages from the extradata.
+
+@item frame_packing_type
+Set frame_packing_arrangement_type (H.265 table D.8).
+
+@table @samp
+@item side_by_side
+@item top_bottom
+@item temporal
+@end table
+
+Default is to take it from the Stereo 3D side data.
+
+@item frame_packing_view
+Set content_interpretation_type: which view the first frame of the arrangement
+is.
+
+@table @samp
+@item unspecified
+@item left_first
+@item right_first
+@end table
+
+Default is to take it from the Stereo 3D side data, left first without any.
+
+@item frame_packing_quincunx
+Set quincunx_sampling_flag. Default is to take it from the Stereo 3D side data;
+it must be zero for temporal interleaving.
+
 @item level
 Set the level in the VPS and SPS.  See H.265 section A.4 and tables
 A.6 and A.7.
